title: technical
pid: 0041146d-192c-4152-a069-db8944bbe7d0
body: |2-
  Think of others' writing as overlapping trees.
  If the writer isn't a graph user, each part of their writing
  is probably located "in only one place".
  But you can see the Platonic truth (e.g. "farming in China"
  is about farming and China, even if you read about it in a book about China
  that wasn't about farming per se) and you can represent it in your graph.
